check.evidence:
I compared the branch with the spec, not with the builder's report. I read §0 (0.2 and R1-R11), §2.3, §3.5-3.6, §4.0-4.1, §4.10-4.14, §5.1-5.4, §6.1-6.10, §7.2, §10.2 S4, §12 and the appendix, and the whole diff 0dbb89a..1fe818f (9 commits, author eval-apply-labs, trailers correct, worktree clean).

Scope: every §10.2 S4 item is done and correct, and so is the orchestrator's earlier-network refusal for the snapshot, sign log and pin. Deviations 1-12 are justified. Deviation 3 (the anchor counts only the commit's own votes) is needed: without it a forged header that covers pads lets the real anchor votes vouch, and then 23 signature checks run. With it, 0 run. Nothing from a later slice is half-built.

Suite, run by me on a copy of 1fe818f (<scratch>/p2-scratch/verify-S4-suite; logs in <scratch>/p2-scratch/verify-S4-logs/suite-run.log and suite-ui.log):
- gofmt -l: no output (also on the worktree).
- go vet and go build, both modules: pass.
- GOLEDGER_CHAOS_SLACK=4 go test -race -count=1 ./..., twice: pass (consensus 57.9/55.5 s, ledger 10.4/10.2 s, node 55.8/56.5 s).
- The same with -C ui, twice: pass (29.8/28.3 s).
- The chaos subset with -count=3: pass (94.5 s).
- Every one of the 9 commits builds and vets in both modules (per-commit.log).

Mutations: 39 mutations in scratch copies (mutations.py, mutations.log). Every spec-listed S4 test and the builder's extra tests fail under their mutation:
- block-hash layout, nonce and power;
- rules 2 and 3, and the proposal-evidence refusal;
- the E38 pin, both in ApplyBlock and in the two intake rules;
- the genesis hash over the accounts digest instead of the state digest, and an unsorted genesis rule;
- the proposer missing from the proposal signature;
- step 6 removed; equivocation, logProposal or relay compared by state digest;
- Consistent without the block hash or the set hash; the anchor counting any vote;
- resolve serving the accounts digest;
- fastForward, the header or the nonce left out;
- the sign log kept, or emptied after a failed write;
- the network-id refusals; the sign log without the block check;
- the 1 MiB proposal route; status without networkId;
- the wallet taking any network, skipping Consistent, or signing for the name; the server signing for the name.

Four mutations survived; they are the test gaps in the problem list (GenesisHash wiring, locked height, first-use verify, pin name). Probes that close them are in <scratch>/p2-scratch/verify-S4-adv/node/zz_verify_s4_test.go and <scratch>/p2-scratch/verify-S4-adv/ui/zz_verify_s4_test.go. They pass at head and fail under their mutations.

Adversarial probes, all passing at head:
- A block carrying every content kind keeps its signed hash through JSON decode and a relay's re-encode. Its strings include `<&>`, U+2028/2029, U+FFFD and control characters; it has nil and empty slices and nil amounts.
- A sign log holding a block with a payment reloads at Open.

Checks by reasoning:
- onProposal runs §4.11 in order, and only a taken proposal is relayed.
- A flood of swapped-body copies costs no more than the existing flood of bogus signatures.
- The committed view equals the live state at every event boundary, so admitPayment can use it.
- Real Phase 1 and S3 snapshot and sign-log JSON decode cleanly and reach the 'earlier network' refusal. A bare-list pin is refused the same way.
- The empty sign log is written only after a fsynced snapshot.
- No blocker or major found.

Demo smoke test on free ports 39431/39432:
- /hdls/status serves networkId village/216c…;
- resolve answers the committed height 7 and the state digest;
- the wallet pinned the id and the founder;
- the record routes answer 200 with an empty body;
- the checkpoint keys are State, LastBlock, Commit and Validators.

